rth of Cincinnati. He secured renomination, has raised about $661,000 with roughly $530,000 on hand, and has already defeated Vanessa Enoch four times. Enoch reports under $3,000 on hand and no meaningful fundraising. All ten expert ratings call the race for Republicans, mostly Safe or Solid, and Polymarket prices Davidson's chances near 90%.\n\nThe main uncertainty is the national political environment, which favors Democrats this year and could narrow the margin if it strengthens further. Trump's criticism of Davidson during the primary season exposed some intraparty friction but did not stop his renomination. With no public general-election polling available, the outlook rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets, all of which point the same way: a Likely Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0643, "margin": -9.89}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0683, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0659, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0117, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0326, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0264, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0418, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0406, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -11.5}]}